## Active worker (observability)

Call **`workflow_status({})`** at session start or after delegating — show `statusLine` to the user when `active` is set (e.g. `Active worker: doc-review (reviewing srs/01-overview)`). Details: [ACTIVE-WORKER.md](../ACTIVE-WORKER.md).

## Ambiguous "approve" or "looks good"

`workflow_route` or ask **one** question — **no worker, no approve tool** until answered:

```
Which did you mean?
1. Sign off a document (e.g. srs/01-overview) — formal approval
2. Approve an extracted spec (e.g. SPEC-003) — after generation
3. Go ahead with the plan we discussed — start making changes
4. Mark a comment thread done (e.g. C-012) — feedback addressed
```

| Answer | workflowId | Tool (in worker) |
|--------|------------|------------------|
| 1 | `doc-review` | `review_approve` (after runbook) |
| 2 | `spec-queue` | `spec_approve` |
| 3 | `resolve-task` or generate | `task_approve_plan` |
| 4 | `resolve-comments` | `comments_resolve` |

## Quick gates (workers enforce; you delegate)

| Workflow | Spawn brief | Forbidden in parent |
|----------|-------------|---------------------|
| Document review | `agents/doc-review.md` | `review_approve` without worker ack |
| Generate SRS/BD | `agents/generate-srs.md` | `docs/` writes before `task_approve_plan` |
| Resolve task | `agents/resolve-task.md` | edits before plan yes |
| Comments | `agents/resolve-comments.md` | `review_approve` for threads |

## Generate vs incremental

| Request | workflowId |
|---------|------------|
| "generate SRS", "write chapter 4" | `generate-srs` |
| "add login with Google", "update auth section" | `resolve-task` |
